All integers use little-endian byte order.

Database header:
[name_size: uint8, 8 bits, 1 byte, maximum 255]
[name: name_size bytes, maximum 255 bytes]

Table header (repeated for each table):
[table_name_size: uint8, 8 bits, 1 byte, maximum 255]
[table_name: table_name_size bytes, maximum 255 bytes]
[row_count: uint32, 32 bits, 4 bytes, maximum 4,294,967,295]
[column_count: uint8, 8 bits, 1 byte, maximum 255]
[max_row_size: uint16, 16 bits, 2 bytes, maximum 65,535]

Column header (repeated column_count times):
[column_name_size: uint8, 8 bits, 1 byte, maximum 255]
[column_name: column_name_size bytes, maximum 255 bytes]
[column_type: uint8, 8 bits, 1 byte, maximum type ID 255]

Column type IDs:
1 = INT
2 = STRING
